From cfc1f08718d79c8344e2ff9651ed396e4608ae2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SplitMind <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:26:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(email-watch): opt-in Gmail watch on the Worker cron,
 with a mail_watch provider

When OOMOL_CONNECT_EMAIL_WATCH_CONNECTIONS names gmail:<connection> entries,
the existing every-minute cron checks those accounts for new inbox mail every
OOMOL_CONNECT_EMAIL_WATCH_INTERVAL_MINUTES (default 10) and keeps only machine
mail that needs action (failed deploys, GitHub failures and review requests,
billing or quota warnings, account or security notices) as a deduplicated list.
Unset, the cron makes no D1 query and no Gmail call for the watch.

- Gmail is reached through ActionRunner by a client that allows only
  gmail.get_profile, gmail.list_history and gmail.fetch_message_by_message_id
  with format metadata; anything else is refused before the runner is called.
- fetch_message_by_message_id gains metadataHeaders (valid only with format
  metadata, sent as repeated query parameters).
- A rule matches only when the first Authentication-Results header is from
  mx.google.com with dmarc=pass and header.from equal to the From domain.
- RunActionInput.audit "outcome" records a run row with no input or output
  summary; the watcher uses it, under a new "cron" run-log caller.
- At most 30 Gmail action runs per invocation, a per-connection cursor updated
  by compare-and-set, catch-up runs off-interval, an expired cursor leaves one
  watch_gap item, and a daily retention sweep.
- New built-in mail_watch provider (no_auth): list_pending_mail (read) and
  acknowledge_mail (write), bound to the D1 store at app creation.
- Migration 0019_email_watch.sql (D1 and PostgreSQL).
- The cron builds the smallest runner it needs (catalog, D1 stores, Gmail
  executors, ConnectionService, ActionRunner), not the whole app.

